# The build context is uploaded to the remote builder on every deploy, and
# data/ alone is ~1.8GB of production SQLite. The Dockerfile copies only
# package*.json, src/, ml/tokenizer.js, litestream.yml and
# docker-entrypoint.sh, so everything below is pure upload cost.
#
# Deliberately no `!` negations: a broad pattern that caught one of those
# paths would break the build, and that is not worth the extra few KB.

# Live data and its backups. The real database lives on the fly volume and
# must never be baked into an image.
data/
backups/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal

# Reinstalled in the image by `npm ci --production`
node_modules/

# Operator tooling, not part of the running service
scripts/
query_foals_nenzz.sh
OPERATIONS.md

# Local config
.env
.env.*
*.log
